_🗄️ Data Integrity & Integration_ | _🟠 Major_ | _⚡ Quick win_

**Validate every fleet graph parameter exposed by the generator.**

Environment overrides can alter `appModules`, `universal`, `popular`, or `tailPicks`, yet this check still accepts and records the run as `"fleet"`. Assert all preset values that determine the generated workload.

<details>
<summary>Proposed fix</summary>

```diff
 const expected = FLEET
-  ? { apps: APPS, libs: LIBS, modulesPerLib: MODULES, shape: "skewed", preset: "fleet" }
+  ? {
+      apps: APPS,
+      libs: LIBS,
+      modulesPerLib: MODULES,
+      appModules: 28,
+      shape: "skewed",
+      universal: 5,
+      popular: 10,
+      tailPicks: 2,
+      preset: "fleet",
+    }
   : { apps: APPS, libs: LIBS, modulesPerLib: MODULES, shape: "layered", universal: 1 };
```
</details>

<!-- suggestion_start -->

<details>
<summary>📝 Committable suggestion</summary>

> ‼️ **IMPORTANT**
> Carefully review the code before committing. Ensure that it accurately replaces the highlighted code, contains no missing lines, and has no issues with indentation. Thoroughly test & benchmark the code to ensure it meets the requirements.

```suggestion
console.log(
  `# optimal-stack gate: ${APPS} apps / ${LIBS} libs${FLEET ? " (fleet shape)" : ""}, foundation=${foundationPkg}`,
);
const genOut = sh(
  FLEET
    ? `node scripts/generate.mjs --preset fleet --apps ${APPS} --tsgo-task --clean`
    : `node scripts/generate.mjs --apps ${APPS} --libs ${LIBS} --modules ${MODULES} --universal 1 --tsgo-task --clean`,
  { encoding: "utf8" },
);
// The generator honors env-var overrides (MODULES=20 etc.), which would silently
// change the generated shape while this record still claimed the requested one.
// Its last stdout line is a JSON summary of what it ACTUALLY generated; assert
// the fields this bench hardcodes or reports.
let gen;
try {
  gen = JSON.parse(genOut.trim().split("\n").pop());
} catch {
  throw new Error(`could not parse the generator summary line from:\n${genOut.slice(-400)}`);
}
const expected = FLEET
  ? {
      apps: APPS,
      libs: LIBS,
      modulesPerLib: MODULES,
      appModules: 28,
      shape: "skewed",
      universal: 5,
      popular: 10,
      tailPicks: 2,
      preset: "fleet",
    }
  : { apps: APPS, libs: LIBS, modulesPerLib: MODULES, shape: "layered", universal: 1 };
for (const [k, v] of Object.entries(expected)) {
  if (gen[k] !== v) {
    throw new Error(
      `generated workspace drifted from the requested shape (env override?): ${k}=${gen[k]}, expected ${v} — summary: ${JSON.stringify(gen)}`,
    );
  }
}
```

</details>

<!-- suggestion_end -->

<details>
<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>

```
Verify each finding against current code. Fix only still-valid issues, skip the
rest with a brief reason, keep changes minimal, and validate.

In `@scripts/optimal-gate-bench.mjs` around lines 218 - 246, Update the
expected-value validation around the gen summary in the optimal-stack benchmark
to cover every fleet workload parameter exposed by the generator, including
appModules, universal, popular, and tailPicks, using the preset’s intended
values. Ensure environment-overridden values for any of these fields cause
validation to fail before the run is recorded as the fleet shape, while
preserving the existing apps, libs, modulesPerLib, shape, and preset checks.
```

</details>

